    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> September 1, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>Prepium ("we", "us", or "our") is committed to protecting the privacy of its users. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your personal information when you use our web application, in compliance with the Nigerian Data Protection Regulation (NDPR) 2019 and other applicable data protection laws.</p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Personal Information:</strong> Name, email address, phone number, and any other information you voluntarily provide.</li>
      <li><strong>Account Information:</strong> Username, password, and profile details.</li>
      <li><strong>Usage Data:</strong> IP address, browser type, device type, pages viewed, and referral URLs.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookies & Tracking Technologies:</strong> We use cookies to remember your preferences and to track usage patterns.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>We may use your information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide and maintain our service.</li>
      <li>Process transactions and manage your account.</li>
      <li>Send administrative communications (e.g., account updates, security alerts).</li>
      <li>Offer and improve our services, develop new features, and conduct analytics.</li>
      <li>Send you marketing communications if you have opted in.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Sharing & Disclosure</h2>
    <p>We may share your information with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Service providers and partners who assist us in operating our site.</li>
      <li>Legal authorities when required by Nigerian law or to protect our rights.</li>
      <li>Business transfers or mergers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information to third parties.</p>

    <h2>5. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain user data for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.</p>

    <h2>6. Your Rights & Choices</h2>
    <p>Under the Nigerian Data Protection Regulation (NDPR) 2019, you have the right to access, correct, or delete your personal information. You may also withdraw consent for any specific use, and request a copy of your data in a commonly used electronic format.</p>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>We implement standard security measures to protect your data, including TLS encryption for data in transit and at rest, in accordance with the security requirements of the Nigerian Data Protection Regulation (NDPR) 2019.</p>

    <h2>8. International Users</h2>
    <p>Our services are hosted in the United States. If you are located outside the U.S., please be aware that your information may be transferred to and processed in the U.S. in compliance with the Nigerian Data Protection Regulation (NDPR) 2019 requirements for international data transfers.</p>

    <h2>9. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The "Effective Date" will reflect the latest revision.</p>

    <h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@prepium.com">privacy@prepium.com</a>.</p>
